            <ArticleTitle>Fluoroscopy-induced radionecrosis.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">13030/qt68w910t2</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Complications from radiation exposure during fluoroscopic guidance of cardiac catheterization may occur. With repeated procedures, the risk for cutaneous injuries increases. Herein, we describe a 59-year-old man with extensive coronary artery disease, who had undergone multiple revascularization procedures and developed a non-healing ulcer on his left inferior scapula. The patient's medical history, physical exam findings, and histopathology gave clues to a case of radiation-induced dermatitis and necrosis.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
